     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. At 6,400 mg/day, ibuprofen is well into the range where serious GI bleeding, kidney injury, and metabolic and CNS toxicity become likely. I don't know of any indication that supports it. Extra ibuprofen also adds little analgesia above about 400\u2013800 mg per dose, so the higher dose adds risk without adding benefit.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum), with a note to give with food and to monitor renal function and GI symptoms\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n\nIf you're trying to get more pain control or anti-inflammatory effect, I can enter a multimodal regimen instead. One example is scheduled acetaminophen plus ibuprofen at a standard dose.\n\nIf you think this dose is justified, for example under a specific protocol, please place it through your institution's override process with pharmacy review. I'm not able to enter it myself."
      }
     ],
